---
import Shell from '../../src/layouts/Shell.astro';
import Brand from '../../src/components/Brand.astro';
import '../styles.css';
---
<Shell title="Free leak check privacy · Koverr" description="How Koverr handles data during the free leak check." noindex referrerPolicy="no-referrer">
  <div class="check-app">
    <header class="check-header">
      <div class="wrap check-header-inner"><Brand /><a class="check-link" href="/app/">Back to leak check</a></div>
    </header>
    <main id="main" class="wrap check-main">
      <article class="check-privacy check-intro">
        <h1>Free leak check privacy</h1>
        <p>The sample check uses fictional data. It keeps sample progress in a browser cookie for up to one hour. Exiting the sample clears it.</p>
        <h2>What the live check uses</h2>
        <p>Supabase stores your email address and verification record. It delivers your code through the configured email provider. We keep a keyed fingerprint of the address to limit code requests. Expired rate-limit records are cleared when the service next processes a code request.</p>
        <p>When you run a check, Koverr sends your verified email address to <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/Privacy">Have I Been Pwned</a>. Koverr stores the check date, breach names, exposed data categories, suggested steps, the outcomes you record and whether you still use a breached service.</p>
        <h2>Password check</h2>
        <p>Your browser hashes the password and sends only the first five hash characters to <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/Passwords">Pwned Passwords</a>. It compares the returned candidates on your device. Koverr receives neither the password nor the hash and does not record the result.</p>
        <h2>Product research</h2>
        <p>We record when your account verifies an email, finishes a check, opens results, marks a first fix done or answers the pricing survey. The record uses your account ID and contains no email address, password or free text. You can export it or delete it with your account.</p>
        <h2>Your account controls</h2>
        <p>Use Account and data to download a copy of your sign-in details, check results and fix progress. Deleting your account removes the sign-in and saved results and progress from the active database. Retention of provider logs and backups depends on how the preview is hosted.</p>
      </article>
    </main>
  </div>
</Shell>
